Pocket Print — second hardware session, 2026-10-14
Printer: LX-D02, MAC `a2ff00…` (redacted), host: Chrome on Android via the public name

This run was the verification pass for the previous commit's fixes. Both held:

  * WRAPPING — the text job grew from 67 to 71 packets because the sentence now wraps to
    a second line, and the paper shows "This printer makes a lovely / racket." complete,
    with the period and margin to spare. The clipped "rack" is gone.
  * PACING — the 341-packet photo held ONCE instead of twice, backed off to 23 ms, and
    finished after a single rewind. Same job shape as the previous session, one fewer
    hold. The photo also came back ~2 s faster (14 s vs 15 s).

New in this run: the calibration header prints "384 dots · density 3 · threshold 128", and
the sheet is no longer dithered, so its ruler and ramp show the head rather than our halftone.

What this run exposed: the night photo printed as dense black grain with the shadows
crushed together. That is not a protocol fault — a dark source with no tone curve and a
1-bit head has nowhere to put shadow detail. Auto-levels (2nd/98th percentile stretch) now
runs before halftoning; measured on a synthetic night photo in the browser, black coverage
drops from 90.3% to 77.1%.

